<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios- Sept 9.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios- Sept 9.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on September 6. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		    P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1  Union Gold Mine	 214.29    1.50</p>
<p>2  Mayne Nickless	  185.75    8.21</p>
<p>3  Gold Mines Aust	 153.33    0.23</p>
<p>4  Golden Shamrock	 146.48    1.04</p>
<p>5  Memtec		    130.14   37.26</p>
<p>6  Adel Bton Cement	114.49    1.58</p>
<p>7  T N T		     113.67    1.58</p>
<p>8  Orion Rsc		 103.49    1.78</p>
<p>9  National Food	    90.13    1.37</p>
<p>10 Pete Secu Aust	   79.22    5.72</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p>1  Dominion Min		2.99    0.73</p>
<p>2  Computer Power	    3.22    3.30</p>
<p>3  Parbury Ltd		 5.03    0.59</p>
<p>4  BTR Plc		    5.13    5.06</p>
<p>5  Country Road		5.71    1.40</p>
<p>6  Pac Mutual Aust	   6.75    2.41</p>
<p>7  OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.05    0.84</p>
<p>8  David Jones		 7.14    1.70</p>
<p>9  Galore Grp		  7.35    0.33</p>
<p>10 Templeton Global	  7.42    1.30</p>
